# Patch:        030-extraction-roots
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       multi-stark/src/hax_roots.rs, multi-stark/src/lib.rs
# Hunks:        2
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 4 (aeneas drops a method that no free
#               function calls). Each rooted item is a method, and three are
#               crate-private.
# Cost:         none in a normal build: the module exists only under
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant it adds free
#               functions, each of which calls one item of the crate.
#               No existing body changes.
# Upstreamable: no: the module exists only for the extractor.
# Drop when:    charon orders `--start-from` methods, so that the methods
#               themselves can be roots.
# Test:         lint p3-multi-stark unexpected_cfgs
# Mutation:     the module is gated on a misspelled cfg, so a normal
#               `cargo check` reports `unexpected_cfgs`.
#
# The roots are the verifier's field arithmetic that needs no transcript and no AIR:
#
# - the boundary selectors at a point, one more coordinate folded in, at one row, and at one row behind a prefix;
# - the successor row rebuilt from the opened columns;
# - the number of free coordinates of the zerocheck.
#
# The field stays generic, so the Lean model quantifies over every implementation.
#
diff --git a/multi-stark/src/hax_roots.rs b/multi-stark/src/hax_roots.rs
